    "perplexity": {
      "description": "The Afterglow is KillerStar's highly anticipated second album, released on March 20, 2026, following their critically acclaimed self-titled debut. Founded by Rob Fleming and James Sedge to channel their shared love of '70s art-rock and modern alternative sounds, the band has crafted an album that seamlessly blends glam rock, art rock, hook-laden pop, and even touches of jazz. The record features eight brand new songs that incorporate elements spanning four decades of musical evolution—from '70s glam-rock and '80s pop-rock to '90s synth-pop and '00s ambient—all unified by refined melodies, delicate piano passages, heavy guitar riffs, and tribal drumming that marry together in perfect harmony.\n\nThe album showcases the exceptional musicianship of KillerStar's renowned collaborators, including several David Bowie alumni: Mike Garson on piano, Earl Slick on guitar, and Mark Plati on bass, alongside additional contributions from Gerry Leonard on guitar, Carey Frank on Hammond organ, and The Webb Sisters on backing vocals. From the opening title track to the closing ballad \"Invincible,\" The Afterglow takes listeners on a breathtaking sonic journey that evokes the spirit of Bowie while establishing its own unique identity. The album received strong support from major UK publications including The Times, Mojo, and RnR, with critics hailing it as a \"vibrant and rocking affair\" that's \"spectacularly produced and professionally delivered.\"\n\nThe record confirms that KillerStar's debut success was no one-off, demonstrating the band as one of the most inspired and imaginative musical projects in contemporary British rock. With standout tracks like \"So Easy,\" \"The Rubicon,\" \"There Has To Be A Reason,\" and \"You Do Me No Favours,\" the album balances high-tempo rock moments and glam-inflected grooves with expansive, atmospheric pieces, all anchored by killer hooks and lyrical themes exploring life, love, and remembrance.",
      "generated_at": "2026-04-06T15:54:29.090475",
